            "LinBiolinumTB"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "End-to-end Software Development",
          "bbox": [
            68.48,
            394.42,
            225.48,
            404.38
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinBiolinumTB"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "End-to-end software development encompasses the entire process of creating a software product.",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            408.84,
            441.71,
            418.8
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.97
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "While conventional code generation is often limited to producing isolated components such as",
          "bbox": [
            45.35,
            420.8,
            440.17,
            430.76
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.06
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "functions, classes, or modules, end-to-end development starts from high-level software requirements",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            432.75,
            440.17,
            442.71
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.86
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and progresses through design, implementation, testing, and ultimately delivering a fully functional",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            444.71,
            440.17,
            454.67
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.86
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and ready-to-use product.",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            456.66,
            150.96,
            466.62
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In practice, developers and stakeholders typically adopt established software process models to",
          "bbox": [
            55.79,
            468.62,
            440.17,
            478.58
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.94
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "guide collaboration, such as Agile [26] and Waterfall [105]. Similarly, the design of LMA systems",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            480.57,
            440.17,
            490.53
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96,
            9.98
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "for end-to-end software development draws inspiration from these software process models. The",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            492.53,
            440.17,
            502.49
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.97
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "development process is organized into distinct phases, such as requirements gathering, software",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            504.48,
            440.17,
            514.45
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.01
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "design, implementation, and testing. Each phase is managed by specialized agents with domain",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            516.44,
            440.17,
            526.4
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.06
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "expertise.",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            528.39,
            84.77,
            538.36
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "It is important to note that works such as FlowGen [81] and Self-Collaboration [31] emulate",
          "bbox": [
            55.79,
            540.35,
            440.17,
            550.31
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96,
            10.06
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "various software process models. However, their experiments focus on generating code segments",
          "bbox": [
            45.58,
            552.3,
            440.17,
            562.27
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "rather than delivering fully developed software products. As a result, in this paper, these approaches",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            564.26,
            440.17,
            574.22
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.86
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "are not considered to be designed for true end-to-end software development.",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            576.21,
            357.51,
            586.18
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Several works [33, 47, 48, 109, 112, 114, 155, 162] adopt the Waterfall model to automate software",
          "bbox": [
            55.79,
            588.17,
            440.17,
            598.13
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.86,
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "development. The Waterfall model used in these multi-agent methods organizes the software",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            600.12,
            440.17,
            610.09
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.06
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "development process into distinct, sequential phases, where each stage must be completed before",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            612.08,
            440.17,
            622.04
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.95
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "proceeding to the next. The primary phases typically include Requirement Analysis, Architecture",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            624.03,
            440.17,
            634.0
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.94
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Design, Code Development, Testing, and Maintenance. For instance, in MetaGPT [48], the Product",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            635.99,
            440.17,
            645.95
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "LinLibertineT"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.89,
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Manager agent thoroughly analyzes user requirements. The Architect agent then transforms these",
          "bbox": [
            45.83,
            647.94,
